    "answer": "例如本船與他船發生碰撞，則僅需敘述碰撞發生前我船之事實狀態、碰撞時 間地點、他船名稱、碰撞位置等即可，對於兩船是否曾採取何種避碰措施或 是過失比例，因恐與日後調查判定法律責任有關，切勿任意載於海事報告 中。又如船舶因意外毀損港埠設施者，則僅需說明船舶於何地、何時、何種 作業狀態下與何種港埠設施發生接觸造成碰損事實即可，無須以贅詞或形容 詞詳細說明接觸之力道多寡或接觸方式是否正常恰當等。 For example when a ship has collided with other ship, then only needs to narrate the collision fact of condition, the time of collision, the place, the opponent ship’s name, the collision position and so on, regarding two ships whether adopt prevent action or the liability judgement to the error proportion. To avoid miss lead to the investigation or determination legal liability in the future. Do not arbitrarily to write in the sea protest. As well as when the ships have accident damages to the port facility, then only need to explain that the ships location, under what kind of job status do have the contact with, what kind of port facility caused damage. Do not use the superfluous word or the adjective to write in detail such as how much the hit power, the way of contact, whether appropriate or not and so on. 當意外或非常事變之事實發生後，船長未必能夠立即發現並確定所有之事實 結果，因此在做成海事報告時通常會加入保留權益(reserving rights)等文 句，如此一來若某事實所造成之結果係日後才被發現者，仍可以做成新的海 事報告載明造成損失之原事實內容。 When after an accident or an unusual case happened, the master couldn’t find and verify all things and all facts. Therefore when the master make the sea protest often add words or sentences to reserving rights, as the result when some outcome be found thereafter, it still has a chance to add a new sea protest to explain the relative new loss and damage found.",
    "source": "船隊行政作業手冊 2026/07-1｜第十五章 海技部相關規範｜第十節 海事報告書、事實陳述書、索賠通知函與常用事故｜PDF 第 187 頁｜手冊 15-63"
