    "answer": "通常為碼頭工頭發現貨櫃外觀異常時，通知值班船員到現場確認並拍照佐 證，由工頭提供貨櫃受損單予大副簽署。 Usually, foreman will provide the Container and Equipment Interchange Receipt Damage Report to Chief mate for signing while they found the container was abnormal, and they will notify duty officer to go to the scene to confirm and take photos. 若有不可抗力因素以致無法到碼頭邊確認櫃損狀況時，大副應根據實際櫃況 在櫃損單內予以加註並使用”Receipt only without admission of any liability” 等字句以確保公司權益。 If there was force majeure event that makes it impossible to go to the shore side to confirm the damage of the container, Chief mate should add a note in the Container and Equipment Interchange Receipt Damage Report based on the actual condition, and use wording such as \"Receipt only & without admission of any liability\" to protect the company's rights and interests. 以下三種情況為常見的情形，大副可依據範例參考加註，但不僅限於範例內 容，如有特別情況亦可再詳盡描述。 The following three situations are very often. Chief mate can refer to the sample and make a note, but it is not limited to the content of the sample, and can be described in more details if there are any other or special circumstances.",
