    "answer": "Below are six examples of CLAIM LETTER. It must be noted that the first (Sample 1) is to directly deliver the \"Notice of Claim\" signed by the captain of the other party. When it is inconvenient for the captain to deliver it in person, the second (Sample 2) is a \"letter\" to his agent. The purpose is to request the agent to deliver the third (Sample 3) \"Notice of Claim\" to the other captain for signature. If you have received the claim letter from the other party, you must never sign it. At most, you can sign for it. Please add \" Receipt Only & Without Any Admission of Liability \" (Receipt notification but no liability issues).",
