    "text": "According to Discharge standard for water pollutants from ships\n(GB3552-2018), recently the China MSA has strengthened the inspection of\nSewage Treatment Plant (STP) for calling ships, and will take and analyses the\ndomestic sewage sample. If there is any non-compliance, the master and chief\nengineer need to go to the MSA to make relevant transcripts and a fine may be\nissued. In the worst case, the ship may be detained. Two of Company fleet\nvessels were inspected at CNNSS & CNNGB and against this Regulation as\nthe MSA officers found that the storm valve of sewage was in OPEN position.\nHereby reiterate and remind all ships to strictly manage the sewage on the ship.\nPlease follow below instructions:\n依據中國船舶水污染物排放控制標準的要求下(GB3552-2018)，近期中國\n各港海事局已加強對於靠港船舶，檢查生活污水處理設備(STP)，並抽取\n生活污水樣品帶回檢查，若有不符合規定者，船長及輪機長需到海事局製\n作相關筆錄並將開罰，情節嚴重者可能導致扣船，同行船舶(馬士基)已被\n開罰 10 萬人民幣 (公司兩艘屬輪分別於南沙及寧波接受檢查，在港期間，\n因生活污水排海防浪閥(storm valve)未關閉，已違反中國船舶水污染物排\n放控制標準)，在此重申並提醒各輪嚴格管控船上生活污水，以下注意事\n項請遵照辦理：\n1. When ship berthed at Chinese port, it is forbidden to discharge sewage. The\nthree-way valve of sewage (or called “gate valve” in different type of ship)\nshall not be placed in discharging overboard position. During staying in\nChina’s waters (extended 3 nautical miles from the coast), the ship’s\nthree-way valve at the sewage treatment plant and the storm valve must be\nclosed and locked. After leaving the China baselines 12 nautical miles,\noutside China waters, please follow normal discharge operation in\naccordance with IMO regulations. (Refer to Discharge Standard for Water\nPollutants from Ships/attachment 5.1.1 & 5.1.2)\n在港期間生活污水禁止排外，生活污水三向閥，絕不可繞過生活污水處\n理設備擺在排海位置。屬輪於中國水域期間(領海基線 3 海里內)，生活\n污水處理設備處的三通轉換閥 (部份船舶是 gate valve)，與生活污水的\n排海防浪閥，需全部在關閉位置並上鎖。離開中國沿岸 12 海里後的其\n他非中國水域，請依照 IMO 規定正常排放。(參閱中國船舶水污染物排\n放控制標準/附件 5.1.1 以及 5.1.2)\n1.1 When in port and within 3 nautical miles (including) from the nearest\nland, the direct discharge of sewage into waters is prohibited.\n在港以及離岸 3 海里內，生活污水無論如何禁止排外。\nThe three-way valve of sewage shall not be placed in discharging"
