    "text": "利用生物系統的生活污水處理設備必須進行定期維護，如果維護不當或\n使其失衡，曝氣室(化糞池)內的微生物將死亡並且性能會降低。\nAfter cleaning STP every month, and the STP must be operated 7 days\nbefore entering Chinese waters. The blower is continuously operated to\nsupply oxygen to cultivate live bacteria (microorganisms). The incubation\nperiod (period in which the microorganisms are generated and stabilized) is\napproximately one week.\n每個月清洗 STP 之後，且進入中國水域之前 7 天就要將 STP 運行起來，\n鼓風機持續運轉供給氧氣以培養活菌 (微生物)。潛伏期（產生並穩定\n微生物的時期）大約為一周。\nAnnex IV of MARPOL\nMARPOL 附錄 IV\nAnnex IV contains a set of regulations regarding the discharge of sewage into\nthe sea, ships' equipment and systems for the control of sewage discharge, the\nprovision of facilities at ports and terminals for the reception of sewage, and\nrequirements for survey and certification. It also includes a model International\nSewage Pollution Prevention Certificate to be issued by national shipping\nadministrations to ships under their jurisdiction.\n附錄四包含一系列有關向海中排放生活污水，船舶控制污水排放的設備和系\n統，在港口和碼頭提供設施以接收污水的規章，以及檢驗和發證的要求。它\n還包括由國家船運管理部門向其管轄範圍內的船舶頒發的國際防止生活污水\n污染證書範本。\nIt is generally considered that on the high seas, the oceans are capable of\nassimilating and dealing with raw sewage through natural bacterial action and\ntherefore the regulations in Annex IV of MARPOL 73/78 prohibit ships from\ndischarging sewage within a specified distance of the nearest land, unless they\nhave in operation an approved treatment plant.\n人們普遍認為，在公海，海洋能夠通過自然細菌作用吸收和處理生活污水，\n因此，《73/78 防污公約》附錄四中的規定禁止船舶在距最近陸地特定距離內\n排放生活污水，除非他們擁有經批准的處理設備。\nThe law requires that existing ship shall be equipped with at least one of the\nfollowing three equipments:\n依法規定，現有船舶應配備以下三種設備中的至少一種：\nExisting ships will be required to comply with the provisions of the revised Annex"
