    "text": "categorized. It need to be listed as a total estimated amount, time/date, position\nand recorded in the “Category” column. Master and C/O must sign to verify.\n(五) 泊靠碼頭或進塢期間，若安排垃圾岸收，紀錄上只可以記錄於岸收的欄位\n中，絕對不可同時記錄於傾倒入海及岸收兩個欄位。\nWhen at berth or at drydock, if arranged by reception facilities, the record\nshould only be recorded in the discharge to reception facilities column.\nConcurrently recorded in the discharge into sea and reception facilities is\nstrictly prohibited.\n(六) 焚燒紀錄欄位，只有焚化爐已取得 IMO type approval certificate 的船舶(2000\n年 1 月 1 日後安裝焚化爐於船上者)並實際使用者才須留有記錄。機艙實際\n使用焚化爐所登記在油料紀錄簿中的數量(單位：立方米)，須同步登記在\n垃圾紀錄簿上。\nShipboard incinerator shall possess IMO type approval certificate only applied\nto the incinerator installed onboard on or after 1st Jan. 2000. The incineration\ncolumn should be recorded when the incinerator is using. Any incinerated\nquantity recorded in the “Oil Record Book” should be concurrently recorded in\nthe “Garbage Record Book” (Unit: cubic meter)\n(七) 船上每天開伙故或多或少均會產生食物廢棄物，故紀錄上不可遺漏，泊靠\n碼頭期間不可直接排海，除非該碼頭有安排岸收作業並備有垃圾收據或證\n明。\nThe discharge record for food waste from the galley should not be omitted.\nWhen at berth, it is strictly prohibited from discharging overboard directly,\nexcept it is received by shore facilities and with receipt or certificate specifying\nthe estimated amount of garbage transferred.\n(八) 港口國檢查最常檢查第 1 類塑膠類如保特瓶之岸收與產出是否合理，請依\n航程總時間、船員總人數、產出量及上次岸收時間，合理估算最正確的數\n量並留存於船上備查。\nCategory 1, Plastic, is usually inspected by PSC especially the reasonable\nquantities of plastic bottles. The quantity of the plastic bottles must match the\ndaily consumption of total crew remained onboard, in addition to the\nconsideration of total sailing time and from the last time of receipt.\n(九) 雖船上可依垃圾拋棄規定摘要表選擇將垃圾以海拋方式處理，但為保護海\n洋環境，屬輪在航線上應儘量選擇可免費提供岸收服務之港口收受設備，\n處理各類垃圾，並請其提供收據或證明以備檢查。\nAlthough discharging the garbage into sea, according to summary of at sea\ngarbage disposal regulations, is allowed. However, for protecting the marine\nenvironment, please choose the free service of garbage discharge reception"
