    "text": "facilities as much as possible at your routine service, with the receipt of\ncertificate for inspection in future.\n(十) 垃圾紀錄簿上登記的項目及數量，應與港口收受垃圾之單據或證明相符，\n並應分別建檔存查。\nThe items and quantities recorded in the “Garbage Record Book” should match\nthe items and quantities recorded in the garbage receipt or certificate, and make\nfiles separately.\n(十一)垃圾紀錄簿由大副負責保管與記錄，不可委託他人，每次處理完一筆紀錄\n後，必須立即在”證明/簽名”欄位上簽字，而每完成一頁的紀錄後，必須交\n由船長簽字確認。\nChief Officer is in charge of keeping and recording the “Garbage Record Book”\nand cannot assign to anybody else. When each time completing one discharge\nof garbage, Chief Officer has to sign his/her name on the\n“certification/signature” column. When completing the last record for each\ncertain page, it should be given to Master for signature and verification.\n(十二)依 MARPOL Annex V 公約規定，垃圾卸岸收據或證明應至保存於船上二\n年，但為配合公司安全管理證書(SMC)外稽檢查時間(中檢每二年半，不長\n於三年)，該垃圾收據或證明和垃圾紀錄簿均須保存於船上三年，即使船上\n已使用新版本，但舊紀錄仍須繼續保存三年，不可提早丟棄。\nAccording to the requirements of MARPOL Annex V, the receipts or\ncertificates must be kept on board the ship with the “Garbage Record Book” for\ntwo years. However, for compliance with the inspection period of Safety\nmanagement Certificate (SMC), every 2.5 years for intermediate audit and not\nlonger than 3 years, the receipts or certificates must be kept on board the ship\nwith the “Garbage Record Book” for 3 years. Old records should be kept on\nboard for three years and not discarded even if new version has been adopted.\n(十三)大副記載於垃圾紀錄簿上的任何資料及數字務必小心，避免塗改；萬一登\n記有誤，請使用原子筆將更正處劃上刪除線後，並在旁邊簽字負責。\nChief Officer must be careful about the entry of any data and figures. Try best\nnot to write over. If case of mis-entry, please use ball-point pen to make a cross\nline underneath it, and Chief Officer to sign his/her name beside for\nresponsibility."
