    "text": "第八節 美國航線注意事項\n一、 適用範圍 Area of application\n本指引闡明公司對船上人員的要求，以期航行美國港口之船舶符合美國聯\n邦政府及加州政府對安全和保護海洋環境的要求，使船舶得以順利泊靠美\n國港口，並通過美國海岸防衛隊及各相關單位之檢查。同時也闡明公司實\n施安全管理系統應負責之部門及人員。\nThis guideline defines the Company's requirements relating to shipboard\noperations, as stipulated in United States of America and the State of\nCalifornia, should be complied with, so as to meet with the USCG and various\nparties’ inspections, and to achieve safe navigation and to protect the marine\nenvironment. It applies to ships scheduled to call at US ports under\nmanagement, Departments and the personnel responsible for implementing the\nSMS of the Company.\n二、 參考目標 References\n美國聯邦法規 CFR: Code of Federal Regulations\n美國加州法規,及 CCR: California Code of Regulations, and\n國際船舶污染預防公約, International conventions of MARPOL &\n海上人命安全公約等國際公約 SOLAS, etc\n三、 職權與責任 Authorities and responsibilities\n（一） 公司指定負責人，船務部主管應負責確認有關公司安全管理系統，美\n國加州及美國聯邦政府所要求之各項船舶作業均已確實施行。\nThe Company DP, Head of Marine Division are responsible for ensuring\nnecessary shipboard operations relating to the specific regulations\nstipulated in United States of America, the State of California, as well as\nSMS of the Company are carried out.\n（二） 各輪船長負責確認有關安全與環境保護方面的各項船舶作業均已確實\n在船上實施，並記錄其結果。\nThe Fleet Master is responsible for ensuring necessary shipboard\noperations on board relating to the safety and protection of the\nenvironment are carried out, and for recording the results.\n（三） 輪機長和大副分別負責協助船長對機艙部人員及甲板部人員推動有關\n安全與環境保護方面各項必要的船舶作業。\nThe Chief Engineer and the Chief Officer are responsible for assisting the\nMaster to carry out shipboard operations relating to the safety and\nprotection of the environmental involving both the deck and the engine\ncrew."
