    "chapter": "第十五章 海技部相關規範",
    "text": "According to 33CFR 164.25, the both deck/engine, including testing\nsteering gear, G/E, M/E, internal communication and vessel control alarm,\nand storage batteries must be tested and record in the Deck/Engine logbook\ntwelve hours before arrival US waters.\n2. 最遲一定要在前往美國的最後一個港口，完成船上 e-NOA/NOD 軟體之\n安裝，至少於港 96 小時前向 National Vessel Movement Center (NVMC)\nenoad@nvmc.uscg.gov 以 e-Mail，並同時副本知會美國分公司/代理行。\nThe software for e-NOA/NOD must be installed onboard not later than the\nlast port of call before departing for US. The initial e-NOA must be sent off\nat least 96 hours before arrival at LGB/LAX via e-mail to National Vessel\nMovement Center (NVMC) enoad@nvmc.uscg.gov and c.c to US\noffice/agent as well.\n3. ETA 或 ETD 如有變動超過+/- 六個小時，請立即以 e-Mail 重發給 NVMC\n及美國公司/代理行。\nHowever, once ship reported and arrival or departure time changes with\nmore than 6 hrs +/-, please update it to the authority, same as the above (b)\naccordingly.\n4. 當下一港口亦是美國港口時 (US port to US port)，船長須於開航前 24\n小時之前發送 Initial US to US e-NOA 至 NVMC 及美國公司/代理行。(以\nCTP Service 為例，即為 LGB-OAK)\nWhen next calling port is also US port (US port to US port), the master is\nresponsible to send Initial US to US e-NOA 24 hours before departure to the\nauthority, same as the above (b) accordingly. (Example will be like\nLGB-OAK for CTP service)\n5. 船長可於 Cut-Off 美國最後一港口前一小時發送 e-NOD 至 NVMC 及美\n國公司/代理行。\nThe e-NOD is requested to be sent off within one hour prior the ship’s\n“Cut-Off” from the last port of United States, same as the above (b)\naccordingly.\n（四） 求生及滅火操演及與 QI 進行雙向演練\nAbandon ship / fire drill & QI Notification Exercise\n1. 棄船操演：施放棄船警報信號，再輔以廣播說明，同仁則依據部署表攜\n帶裝備及文件迅速集合，因顧及意外與人員安全，目前 USCG 並不要\n求船員登上小艇而僅只進行下放與收回之操作。要以英文說明任務及替\n代人的任務。\nAbandon ship drill: Push the abandon ship signal followed by broadcast.\nMuster crew at their stations according to Muster List. Check whether the"
