    "chapter": "第十五章 海技部相關規範",
    "text": "If bunkering at US ports, before arrival, please e-mail to CHGMS via\ninfo@chgms.com. All the pre-bunkering meeting must be well conducted in\nadvance. Engine crew should be capable of speaking his duty and\nemergency dialogues in simple English.\n2. 加油時，各職司人員依加油部署表的規定佈署，USCG 會以望遠鏡在遠\n處監視船上的一舉一動，若發現當值人員離開現場，會拍照存證重罰。\n不得有酗酒現象，其他請參考加油注意事項。\nDuring bunkering, the assigned crew should be deployed according to the\ntable of oil spill station. USCG will monitor from afar by telescope, and\nphotos of penalty will be given if found duty crew not standby and is\nleaving from the bunker station. Assigned crew at duty is strictly banned\nfrom drinking alcohol. For more information, please refer to ISM bunkering\nprocedures.\n3. 油污染應急設備 12 barrel，將由物料課供船，請船上做好存量管理並張\n貼設備清單於現場。進行加燃油時應將木屑，破布及吸油棉片等放置現\n場，以備油污發生。\nSupply section will furnish 12 barrels of oil spill kit to your ship. Please\nmake good inventory control and post the inventory list at scene. During\nbunkering, please prepare saw dust, cotton rags and sponge mates at scene\netc to prevent oil pollution.\n4. 自 2014 年 1 月 1 日起，美國加州水域內和基線 24 海浬內的所有主機、\n輔機、鍋爐都必須轉換使用含硫量低於 0.1%的船用輕柴油(DMA / 即\nMGO)或 0.1%的船用柴油(DMB / 即 MDO)，相關換油的日期、時間及\n船舶經緯度必須詳加記載在甲板/機艙日誌簿及相關記錄上，以備查驗\n(紀錄表單，在本節的最後)。自 2012 年 8 月 1 日起，進入(ECA)北美限\n制排放區域 200 海浬，船舶燃油(IFO)含硫量必須低於 1%並備妥相關文\n件備查。\nThe regulations for all vessels within California Waters and within 24\nNautical Miles from the baseline to use Marine Gas Oil (DMA / i.e. MGO)\nat or below 0.1 % Sulphur content or Marine Diesel Oil (DMB / i.e. MDO)\nat or below 0.1%. Sulphur content in all Main Engines and Auxiliary Diesel\nEngines and Auxiliary Boilers have been effective from 01 JAN. 2014. The\nswitchover procedure from high to low sulphur diesel oil must be adopted\nand must record the relevant date, time, and ship position in the\nDeck/Engine logbook for inspection, as required (relevant forms as attached\nto this chapter).Since 01 AUG 2012, all vessels need to use fuel oil (IFO) at\nor below1.0% sulphur content when operating inside 200 miles of North"
