    "chapterNo": 15,
    "chapter": "第十五章 海技部相關規範",
    "text": "6. 索賠函(CLAIM LETTER)\n索賠函是在商務活動中當出現爭議糾紛後，受損方為了維護權益和解決問題\n而用書面形式向違約一方提出索賠要求的信函。之所以寫索賠函，是想通過\n協商來解決問題，因此寫索賠函前一定要分清是非責任，收集足夠證據，撰\n寫時注意措辭和語氣的禮貌，促使事態朝有利於索賠的方向發展。\nIf there have a dispute happened during the commercial activity, a claim letter is\na letter using for demand to the damaged party’s representative holding them\nresponsible to protect rights and solve problems. The reason for writing the claim\nletter is to resolve the problem through negotiation. Therefore, before writing the\nclaim letter, you must distinguish what the problem is. Collect sufficient\nevidence, and pay attention to the politeness of the wording and tone when\nwriting, so as to promote the development of the situation in the direction of the\nclaim.\n如果是收到對方的 Claim Letter，絕不可簽認，最多只是簽收，請加註\n“Receipt only & without any admission of liability”(收到通知，但無涉責任\n問題)。\nIf you have received the claim letter from the other party, you must never sign it.\nAt most, you can acknowledge by writing “Receipt only & without any\nadmission of liability” (Receipt notification but no liability issues).\n附件提供幾則英文海事報告範例供船長參考：\nEnclosures are some samples of the main text in sea protest for reference:\n1. 海事報告書&事實陳述書範例\nSamples of Sea Protest/ Marine note of protest & Statement of fact.\nSample 1: Collided with other vessel.\nSample 2: Vessel encountered bad weather.\nSample 3: Vessel touched shore crane.\nSample 4: Crew injured.\nSample 5: Stevedore injured.\nSample 6: Stevedore damage to Vessel’s Mast.\n2. 海事報告書之延續範例\nSample of Extended Marine Note of Protest.\n3. 碼頭作業工人造成損害報告範例(亦可參見 ISM FM-0704-2)\nSamples of Stevedore Damage Report. (Also refer to ISM FM-0704-2)\n4. 索賠通知函範例\nSamples of CLAIM LETTER."
